! Triplet O2 in a box: the Berry-phase polarization at nspin = 2 where the two
! channels hold different numbers of bands, seven up and five down.
!
! The ground state is `o2-fixed-lsda.in` beside this file, run first by pw.x
! with the same (default) prefix; this input is the `lberry` run on top of it,
! one string of four points along b_3 (nppstr counts the repeated endpoint, so
! three distinct points). Both channels are gapped: up fills through the pi*
! pair, down stops below it.
!
! The case is chosen because the channels differ. At tot_magnetization = 0 the
! two channels are one channel twice, and a code that solved channel 0 twice,
! or filled both to the same depth, reads the same as pw.x; here it does not.
! AlAs at tot_magnetization = 2 was tried first and is unusable: its down
! channel of three bands cuts the p-like triplet at Gamma, and pw.x prints a
! string phase of exactly 0.00000 where the overlap determinant vanished.
 &control
    calculation = 'nscf'
    lberry = .true.
    gdir = 3
    nppstr = 4
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 10.0,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    nbnd = 9,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0,
    occupations = 'fixed',
    nspin = 2,
    tot_magnetization = 2,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 O  15.99994  O.pz-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (bohr)
 O 0.00 0.00 0.00
 O 0.00 0.00 2.30
K_POINTS (automatic)
 1 1 4 0 0 0
